From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:42:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refresh: use std::this_thread::yield() in noop() on riscv64

noop() spins with _mm_pause() on Windows, std::this_thread::yield() on
aarch64, and falls back to __builtin_ia32_pause() everywhere else, so
any non-x86 non-aarch64 GCC build stops at:

    utils.h:18:25: error: '__builtin_ia32_pause' was not declared in
    this scope; did you mean '__builtin_riscv_pause'?

Take the aarch64 branch on riscv64 too. <thread> is already included
by active_thread_pool.h ahead of utils.h, as for aarch64.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; refresh-bio/FAMSA master still has the x86-only fallback]
---
 libs/refresh/active_thread_pool/lib/utils.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/refresh/active_thread_pool/lib/utils.h b/libs/refresh/active_thread_pool/lib/utils.h
index 27acbbb..e29515b 100644
--- a/libs/refresh/active_thread_pool/lib/utils.h
+++ b/libs/refresh/active_thread_pool/lib/utils.h
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ namespace refresh
 		{
 #if defined(_WIN32)
 			_mm_pause();
-#elif defined(__aarch64__)
+#elif defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__riscv)
 			std::this_thread::yield();
 #else
 			__builtin_ia32_pause();
-- 
